        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "add per-conversation whatsapp debounce config",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nThe existing WhatsApp debounce setting is too broad for mixed usage.\n\nSome conversations should be processed immediately, while others should wait briefly so OpenClaw can batch several short messages into one agent turn. This matters for owner chats, external direct chats, and busy groups that need different timing.\n\nAI-assisted: yes, Codex helped update this branch and evidence.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nThis adds per-conversation inbound debounce settings for WhatsApp direct chats and groups while keeping the existing channel-level debounce as the fallback.\n\nThe runtime now supports:\n\n- `channels.whatsapp.direct[\"<id>\"].debounceMs`\n- `channels.whatsapp.direct[\"*\"].debounceMs`\n- `channels.whatsapp.groups[\"<id>\"].debounceMs`\n- `channels.whatsapp.groups[\"*\"].debounceMs`\n- account-scoped direct/group maps that replace the matching root map for that account\n\n## User Impact\n\nOperators can tune WhatsApp batching per conversation without changing the global WhatsApp debounce for every chat.\n\nExamples:\n\n- owner/admin direct chats can use `debounceMs: 0` for immediate turns\n- external direct chats can wait longer for short message bursts\n- noisy groups can have their own window\n- wildcard entries can set direct/group defaults\n\n## Evidence\n\nCurrent head: `fa74af4f9e07be642ed165858978c88e40c4bde9`\n\nRedacted real WhatsApp setup proof from a local OpenClaw home was already captured for this PR. It used real WhatsApp session keys from the local OpenClaw session index, printed only counts and redacted aliases, and showed:\n\n```text\n0ms real-session-inventory direct=200 group=3\n0ms config <redacted-direct-1> debounceMs=0\n0ms config <redacted-direct-2> debounceMs=120\n0ms config <redacted-group-1> debounceMs=180\n0ms flush <redacted-direct-1> items=1 debounceMs=0\n0ms flush <redacted-direct-1> items=1 debounceMs=0\n151ms flush <redacted-direct-2> items=2 debounceMs=120\n220ms flush <redacted-group-1> items=2 debounceMs=180\n# exit code 0\n```\n\nFocused validation after rebasing on current `origin/main`:\n\n```text\n$ pnpm docs:list\n# exit code 0\n```\n\n```text\n$ node --import tsx scripts/generate-bundled-channel-config-metadata.ts --check\n# exit code 0\n```\n\n```text\n$ node scripts/run-tsgo.mjs -p test/tsconfig/tsconfig.extensions.test.json --incremental --tsBuildInfoFile .artifacts/tsgo-cache/extensions-test.tsbuildinfo\n# exit code 0\n```\n\n```text\n$ node scripts/run-vitest.mjs run --config test/vitest/vitest.runtime-config.config.ts src/config/zod-schema.providers-whatsapp.test.ts\nTest Files  1 passed (1)\nTests       11 passed (11)\n```\n\n```text\n$ node scripts/run-vitest.mjs run --config test/vitest/vitest.e2e.config.ts extensions/whatsapp/src/auto-reply.web-auto-reply.connection-and-logging.e2e.test.ts\nTest Files  1 passed (1)\nTests       29 passed (29)\n```\n\n```text\n$ git diff --check\n# exit code 0\n```\n\n```text\n$ codex review --base origin/main\nI found no discrete correctness issues in the changed debounce configuration, resolution, or inbound debouncer integration.\n```\n",
